{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function queueStrategy(options?): QueueStrategy;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/strategies/queueStrategy.ts#L56","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/strategies/queueStrategy.ts:56"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a queue strategy that processes admitted mutations in order with proper serialization."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unlike other strategies that may drop executions, queue ensures every\nadmitted mutation is attempted sequentially. Each transaction commit completes before\nthe next one starts. Useful when data consistency is critical and\nevery admitted operation must be attempted in order. When a bounded queue is\nfull, the returned transaction fails and its optimistic mutation rolls back.\nCleanup stops new admission. The existing timer drains admitted waiting work\nat its configured pace behind earlier writes. Cleanup does not wait for settlement."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error handling behavior:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a mutation fails, it is NOT automatically retried - the transaction transitions to \"failed\" state"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failed mutations surface their error via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transaction.when('settled')"},{"type":"text","value":" (which will reject)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subsequent mutations continue processing - a single failure does not block the queue"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each mutation is independent; there is no all-or-nothing transaction semantics"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/QueueStrategyOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueueStrategyOptions"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration for queue behavior (FIFO/LIFO, timing, size limits)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/QueueStrategy.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueueStrategy"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A queue strategy instance"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// FIFO queue - process in order received\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: queueStrategy({\n    wait: 200,\n    addItemsTo: 'back',\n    getItemsFrom: 'front'\n  })\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"// LIFO queue - process most recent first\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: queueStrategy({\n    wait: 200,\n    addItemsTo: 'back',\n    getItemsFrom: 'back'\n  })\n})","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction queueStrategy(options?): QueueStrategy;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/strategies/queueStrategy.ts:56](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/strategies/queueStrategy.ts#L56)\n\nCreates a queue strategy that processes admitted mutations in order with proper serialization.\n\nUnlike other strategies that may drop executions, queue ensures every\nadmitted mutation is attempted sequentially. Each transaction commit completes before\nthe next one starts. Useful when data consistency is critical and\nevery admitted operation must be attempted in order. When a bounded queue is\nfull, the returned transaction fails and its optimistic mutation rolls back.\nCleanup stops new admission. The existing timer drains admitted waiting work\nat its configured pace behind earlier writes. Cleanup does not wait for settlement.\n\n**Error handling behavior:**\n- If a mutation fails, it is NOT automatically retried - the transaction transitions to \"failed\" state\n- Failed mutations surface their error via `transaction.when('settled')` (which will reject)\n- Subsequent mutations continue processing - a single failure does not block the queue\n- Each mutation is independent; there is no all-or-nothing transaction semantics\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options?\n\n[`QueueStrategyOptions`](../interfaces/QueueStrategyOptions.md)\n\nConfiguration for queue behavior (FIFO/LIFO, timing, size limits)\n\n## Returns\n\n[`QueueStrategy`](../interfaces/QueueStrategy.md)\n\nA queue strategy instance\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\n// FIFO queue - process in order received\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: queueStrategy({\n    wait: 200,\n    addItemsTo: 'back',\n    getItemsFrom: 'front'\n  })\n})\n```\n\n```ts\n// LIFO queue - process most recent first\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: queueStrategy({\n    wait: 200,\n    addItemsTo: 'back',\n    getItemsFrom: 'back'\n  })\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: queueStrategy\ntitle: queueStrategy\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction queueStrategy(options?): QueueStrategy;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/strategies/queueStrategy.ts:56](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/strategies/queueStrategy.ts#L56)\n\nCreates a queue strategy that processes admitted mutations in order with proper serialization.\n\nUnlike other strategies that may drop executions, queue ensures every\nadmitted mutation is attempted sequentially. Each transaction commit completes before\nthe next one starts. Useful when data consistency is critical and\nevery admitted operation must be attempted in order. When a bounded queue is\nfull, the returned transaction fails and its optimistic mutation rolls back.\nCleanup stops new admission. The existing timer drains admitted waiting work\nat its configured pace behind earlier writes. Cleanup does not wait for settlement.\n\n**Error handling behavior:**\n- If a mutation fails, it is NOT automatically retried - the transaction transitions to \"failed\" state\n- Failed mutations surface their error via `transaction.when('settled')` (which will reject)\n- Subsequent mutations continue processing - a single failure does not block the queue\n- Each mutation is independent; there is no all-or-nothing transaction semantics\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options?\n\n[`QueueStrategyOptions`](../interfaces/QueueStrategyOptions.md)\n\nConfiguration for queue behavior (FIFO/LIFO, timing, size limits)\n\n## Returns\n\n[`QueueStrategy`](../interfaces/QueueStrategy.md)\n\nA queue strategy instance\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\n// FIFO queue - process in order received\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: queueStrategy({\n    wait: 200,\n    addItemsTo: 'back',\n    getItemsFrom: 'front'\n  })\n})\n```\n\n```ts\n// LIFO queue - process most recent first\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: queueStrategy({\n    wait: 200,\n    addItemsTo: 'back',\n    getItemsFrom: 'back'\n  })\n})\n```\n"}
